egetable oil. Place the dough into the bowl and turn until it is covered in the oil. Cover the bowl with cling film and set aside in a warm place for one hour, or until the dough has doubled in size. Lightly grease a baking tray. Incorporate 1.4 oz butter, 1 whole eggs, 1 pinch vegetable oil, 0.9 oz butter, 5 tbsp brown sugar, 2 tsp cinnamon, 10 tbsp dried fruit, 2 tbs milk, and 2 tbs caster sugar smoothly until evenly distributed."}]]}],["$","li","3",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Shape & Layer: Chelsea Buns"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"For the filling, knock the dough back to its original size and turn out onto a lightly floured work surface. Roll the dough out into a rectangle 0.5cm/¼in thick. Brush all over with the melted butter, then sprinkle over the brown sugar, cinnamon and dried fruit. Roll the dough up into a tight cylinder , cut ten 4cm/1½in slice and place them onto a lightly greased baking sheet, leaving a little space between each slice. Cover with a tea towel and set aside to rise for 30 minutes. Preheat oven to 190C/375F/Gas 5."}]]}],["$","li","4",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Bake / Chill: Chelsea Buns"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Bake the buns in the oven for 20-25 minutes, or until risen and golden-brown. Meanwhile, for the glaze, heat the milk and sugar in a saucepan until boiling. Reduce the heat and simmer for 2-3 minutes. Remove the buns from the oven and brush with the glaze, then set aside to cool on a wire rack."}]]}]]}],["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","mochi-donuts",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/recipes/strawberry-glazed-mochi-donuts/","children":"Strawberry Glazed Mochi Donuts"}]}],["$","li","crispy-caramel-croffle",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/recipes/crispy-caramel-croffle/","children":"Crispy Caramel Croissant Waffle (Croffle)"}]}],"$L13","$L14","$L15","$L16"]}]]}]}]
